ARTICLE 2 — PURPOSE AND PERMITTED USE

2.1 Previewer may use the Preview Materials solely for the Purpose. Any other use is prohibited.

2.2 Previewer will not:
  (a) publish, post, blog, tweet, livestream, present at any conference, or otherwise publicly discuss the Preview Model, Model Outputs, or any capability, limitation, or evaluation result, without the Lab's prior written consent;
  (b) share Model Outputs, benchmark results, or any comparison of the Preview Model against any other model (including the Lab's own prior models) in any public forum, research paper, blog post, or social media channel, prior to the Lab's general availability announcement;
  (c) use Model Outputs to train, fine-tune, distill, or otherwise develop any machine learning model, whether open source or proprietary;
  (d) use the Preview Model in any production workload or any application made generally available to end users;
  (e) attempt to extract model weights, tokenizer state, system prompts, or safety configurations, whether by prompt injection, jailbreaking, adversarial techniques, or otherwise;
  (f) reverse engineer, decompile, or otherwise attempt to derive the composition, architecture, or training data of the Preview Model; or
  (g) use the Preview Materials to build, support, or improve any competing foundation model or inference service.

2.3 No Residuals. Previewer's personnel may not rely on "unaided memory" to use Confidential Information outside the Purpose.

ARTICLE 2 — PURPOSE AND PERMITTED USE

2.1 Participant may use the Beta Materials solely for the Purpose. Any other use is prohibited.

2.2 Participant will not:
  (a) redistribute, resell, sublicense, or transfer the Beta Materials to any third party;
  (b) publish, post, blog, tweet, livestream, or otherwise publicly discuss the existence of the beta program, the specifics of the Beta API, or any benchmark, screenshot, or demonstration of the Beta API without Provider's prior written consent;
  (c) reverse engineer, decompile, or attempt to derive the source code of any part of the Beta Materials;
  (d) use the Beta API in any production workload or any application made generally available to end users; or
  (e) build a competing product or service, or use the Beta Materials to train any competing model or service.

2.3 No Residuals. Participant's Representatives may not rely on "unaided memory" to reuse Confidential Information outside the Purpose.
